IMPORT prelude

§ `Codex Insurance Policy -- fact schema, helpers, and coverage rule`

§§ `Fact schema`

-- Verbatim from bench/schema-l4.md, EXCEPT that the multi-word field names inside
-- `DECLARE Claim HAS ...` have been backtick-quoted. schema-l4.md's own header says it is
-- "mechanically derived", and its two supporting-helper GIVEN blocks correctly backtick-quote
-- their multi-word parameters (`` `event month` ``, `` `limit month` ``) -- but the `HAS`
-- block below them left its multi-word field names bare (`agreement signed IS A BOOLEAN`,
-- etc.). An unquoted multi-word span is not a legal L4 identifier -- see
-- doc/reference/syntax/identifier-example.l4, and every multi-word record field anywhere in
-- jl4-core/libraries (e.g. `` `Contract Event` ``'s fields), which are either single
-- camelCase words or backtick-quoted. Quoting here is a pure syntax fix: no field is renamed,
-- added, removed, or retyped. See NOTES.md.

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF Sickness, `Accidental injury`, Neither

DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
  Skydiving, `Military service`, Firefighting, `Police service`, Other

DECLARE Claim
  HAS `agreement signed`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `premium paid month`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hospitalization month`                   IS A NUMBER
      `hospitalization ground`                  IS A Ground
      `age at hospitalization`                  IS A NUMBER
      causes                                    IS A LIST OF Cause
      `fraud month`                             IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `misrepresentation month`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit month`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit provider qualified`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `written confirmation month`              IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `dispute arisen`                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable to settle month`                  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `arbitration commenced month`             IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `valid arbitration award issued`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `written proof of claim month`            IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `recovery sought month`                   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `policy term months`                      IS A NUMBER

§§ `Supporting helpers (verbatim, pre-defined by bench/schema-l4.md -- do not redefine)`

GIVEN  `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
       `limit month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no later than` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m AT MOST `limit month`

GIVEN  cs IS A LIST OF Cause
       c  IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arose out of` MEANS elem c cs

§§ `Additional low-level helpers used by covered`
-- Not equivalents of the two helpers above -- these test presence and relative-gap facts,
-- not no-later-than-a-fixed-limit facts.

GIVEN `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`has occurred` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST v  THEN TRUE

GIVEN `earlier event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `later event month`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `allowed gap`         IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`commenced within period after` MEANS
  CONSIDER `earlier event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST e  THEN
      CONSIDER `later event month`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST l THEN (l MINUS e) AT MOST `allowed gap`

§ `1. Policy in effect and conditions`

§§ `1.1 (preamble) -- hospitalization must be for sickness or accidental injury`
-- A benefit is premised only on hospitalization for sickness or accidental injury;
-- hospitalization for some other reason is not a covered event type at all.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `hospitalization ground`
      WHEN Neither THEN FALSE
      OTHERWISE    TRUE

§§ `1.1(2) -- the premium has been paid`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `premium has been paid` claim IF
    `has occurred` (claim's `premium paid month`)

§§ `1.1(3) / 1.3 -- the wellness-visit condition`
-- Still pending, or satisfied in a timely fashion.
--
-- "No later than the 7th month anniversary ... you will supply ... written confirmation
-- ... of a wellness visit ... occurring no later than the 6th month anniversary." Read
-- together with 1.1(3) ("still pending or has been satisfied in a timely fashion") and
-- 1.2's mirroring cancellation trigger ("has not been satisfied in a timely fashion"), this
-- is a single compound obligation that falls due, as a whole, at the month-7 mark: before
-- month 7 nothing has come due yet ("still pending"), so it cannot yet have failed; at or
-- after month 7 it must actually have been satisfied. See NOTES.md.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wellness visit condition still pending` claim IF
    (claim's `hospitalization month`) LESS THAN 7

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wellness visit condition satisfied in a timely fashion` claim IF
        `no later than` (claim's `written confirmation month`) 7
    AND `no later than` (claim's `wellness visit month`) 6
    AND claim's `wellness visit provider qualified`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wellness visit condition met` claim IF
        `wellness visit condition still pending` claim
    OR  `wellness visit condition satisfied in a timely fashion` claim

§§ `1.2 -- cancellation`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fraud has occurred` claim IF
    `has occurred` (claim's `fraud month`)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `misrepresentation has occurred` claim IF
    `has occurred` (claim's `misrepresentation month`)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `hospitalization within the policy term` claim IF
    (claim's `hospitalization month`) AT MOST (claim's `policy term months`)

-- Item 3 above (the wellness-visit condition) and this "not canceled" item overlap: 1.2's
-- third cancellation trigger ("the condition in 1.3 has not been satisfied in a timely
-- fashion") is the same fact as `wellness visit condition met` above, just double-negated.
-- Both citations are kept, matching the contract's own restatement, rather than deduplicated
-- away.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy has not been canceled` claim IF
    NOT (   `fraud has occurred` claim
        OR  `misrepresentation has occurred` claim
        OR  NOT (`wellness visit condition met` claim)
        OR  NOT (`hospitalization within the policy term` claim)
        )

§ `2. General exclusions`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `excluded under the general exclusions` claim IF
        `arose out of` (claim's causes) Skydiving
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's causes) `Military service`
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's causes) Firefighting
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's causes) `Police service`
    OR  (claim's `age at hospitalization`) AT LEAST 80

§ `3. General conditions`

§§ `3.1 -- worldwide, 24-hour coverage`
-- Purely expansive; imposes no additional condition on `covered`.

§§ `3.2 -- arbitration, and the 60-day pre-suit waiting period`

-- The "unable to settle / arbitration commenced / valid arbitration award" sub-clause is
-- conditional on a dispute having arisen at all.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `dispute has been properly arbitrated` claim IF
    NOT (claim's `dispute arisen`)
    OR  (    `commenced within period after` (claim's `unable to settle month`) (claim's `arbitration commenced month`) 3
         AND claim's `valid arbitration award issued`
        )

-- "In no case shall You seek to recover on this Policy before the expiration of sixty (60)
-- days after written proof of claim has been submitted." This sentence is phrased
-- unconditionally ("in no case"), unlike the dispute/arbitration sentences before it, so it
-- is treated as applying regardless of whether a dispute arose. Every other month-valued
-- fact in this schema is in whole (or half) MONTHS; 60 days is taken as 2 months (60 / 30)
-- for unit consistency -- see NOTES.md. If recovery has not been sought at all, the clause
-- is not yet violated.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`recovery not sought before the waiting period expired` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `recovery sought month`
      WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
      WHEN JUST r  THEN
        CONSIDER claim's `written proof of claim month`
          WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
          WHEN JUST w  THEN r AT LEAST (w PLUS 2)

§ `covered`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE covered claim IF
        `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury` claim
    AND claim's `agreement signed`
    AND `premium has been paid` claim
    AND `wellness visit condition met` claim
    AND `policy has not been canceled` claim
    AND NOT (`excluded under the general exclusions` claim)
    AND `dispute has been properly arbitrated` claim
    AND `recovery not sought before the waiting period expired` claim
